# libc.1 -- the exported ABI of the shared C library.
#
# One linker name per line, trailing `_' included; order is irrelevant.
# Adding a name is always allowed.  Removing, renaming or changing the
# meaning of one breaks installed clients: that needs libc.2.
#
# Left out:
#  * libc's internal state (_mhdr_, _fnclst_, sigtable, __a_*): an export
#    can never be withdrawn.
#  * errno_ and SS: absolutes, identical in every process.
#  * etext_, edata_, end_: defined per program by the linker.
#  * _prof.o refers to etext_; strrchr.o duplicates strchr.c's strrchr_;
#    _finish.o is the no-stdio stub, so clients get finit.c's _finish_.
#
# _slinit_ is not C: crt0sl.s calls it with this program's envp and break.
_canl_
_canw_
_doprnt_
_dtefg_
_dtoa_
_exit_
_fgetb_
_fgetc_
_fgeteof_
_fginit_
_finish_
